  RecordLogin { User => RT::User|RT::CurrentUser }
    Stamps the given user's "Last Login" custom field with the current time.
    Called from the "SuccessfulLogin" callback after a successful password
    login (see
    html/Callbacks/RT-Extension-LastLogin/autohandler/SuccessfulLogin).

    Always re-loads the user as "RT->SystemUser" rather than trusting the
    rights of the user who just logged in - a SelfService/portal user
    normally lacks "SeeCustomField"/"ModifyCustomField" on themselves. Never
    dies: any failure is logged and swallowed, since a broken write here
    must not break the login itself.

  _ShouldSkip { LastValue => STR|undef, MinInterval => SECONDS, Now => UNIX_EPOCH }
    Pure throttle decision, split out of "RecordLogin" so it is unit
    testable without a database: true if "LastValue" parses to a time less
    than "MinInterval" seconds before "Now". "MinInterval" of 0 (the
    default) or a missing/unparseable "LastValue" (first login) never skips.

    Parses "LastValue" with "Format => 'iso'", not 'unknown': the value is
    always one this module wrote itself (via "W3CDTF" in RT::Date), so the
    exact format is known, and 'unknown' would pull in "Time::ParseDate" for
    no reason - RT::Date's own docs call that "a heavyweight operation that
    should never be called from within RT's core".

NAME
    RT::Extension::LastLogin - Records the timestamp of a user's last
    successful login

DESCRIPTION
    Stamps a global "Last Login" custom field on "RT::User" with the current
    time whenever a user successfully logs in through the password login
    form (SelfService/portal or Staff). The value is stored as a standard
    "DateTime" custom field, so it is returned automatically by "GET
    /REST/2.0/user/:id" without any REST2 changes.

    Only password logins
    ("RT::Interface::Web::AttemptPasswordAuthentication") are covered.
    SAML/external-auth logins fire a separate callback
    ("ExternalAuthSuccessfulLogin") that this extension does not hook.

RT VERSION
    Works with RT 6.0.0 and later.

INSTALLATION
    "perl -I. Makefile.PL"
        The "-I." is required: modern Perl does not keep "." in @INC, and
        "use inc::Module::Install" must find the bundled inc/ directory.

    "make"
    "make install"
        May need root permissions.

    Register the "Last Login" custom field
        "make install" does not load etc/initialdata. Run once per RT
        instance:

            /opt/rt/sbin/rt-setup-database --action insert \
                --datafile /opt/rt/local/plugins/RT-Extension-LastLogin/etc/initialdata

    Edit your /opt/rt/etc/RT_SiteConfig.pm
            Plugin('RT::Extension::LastLogin');

    Clear your Mason cache and restart the webserver
            rm -rf /opt/rt/var/mason_data/obj

CONFIGURATION
    All configuration is optional; sensible defaults apply.

  $LastLogin_CustomFieldName
    Name of the custom field to update. Default: "Last Login".

  $LastLogin_RecordTransaction
    If true, also records a transaction on the user for every login (visible
    in the user's history). Default: 0 (update the custom field value only,
    no history entry per login).

  $LastLogin_MinInterval
    Minimum number of seconds between two recorded updates for the same
    user; 0 (default) always updates.

CAVEATS
  Renaming the custom field breaks lookup silently
    "RecordLogin" finds the custom field by the name in
    $LastLogin_CustomFieldName, not by id. Renaming "Last Login" in Admin >
    Custom Fields (without updating the config to match) makes every login
    log a "custom field '...' not found" warning and stop updating the
    timestamp - logins themselves are unaffected, but the data goes stale
    without any user-visible error.

